  {
   "id": "C12",
   "statement": "The prompt-specific advantage in C1 survives on responses the criteria were NOT authored against. Measured as attribution on rubric-blind fresh responses; requires a positive value. FAILS -- but note r13 refutes the response-set-knowledge explanation for that failure: response-blind seed criteria carry more attribution than criteria written after reading the candidates, so the non-transfer is a property of the measurement off distribution, not of what the criteria encode.",
